                                                "sense_id": "ac04273d-9551-3203-914f-8432c36e4f23",
                                                "text": "The identification of the border between England and Scotland always has been a source of interest to railway travellers. For many years, however, the exact points north of Berwick and Carlisle at which the Anglo-Scottish main lines passed from one country to the other were not defined, but the erection of clear and unmistakable lineside signs has put the matter beyond all doubt."
                                            },
